EXT. RIVERBANK - ABANDONED MILL - DAWN

Mist. A rusted waterwheel stands half-sunk in the current. Birdsong where there should be none.

Three soldiers crouch behind a broken wall. Mud to the knees. Eyes red.

SERGEANT MIREILLE DUVAL, 30s, holds a rifle across her knees and watches the far bank.

PRIVATE OSKAR LINDGREN, 19, wrings out a sock. Ruined boots beside him.

A third figure lies on his back under a tarp, only a hand showing. Breath fogs. He is the WOUNDED SOLDIER, 20s, pale, one sleeve soaked dark.

                    OSKAR
(whispering)
Quiet out there.

                    MIREILLE
Too quiet.

                    OSKAR
That's what I said.

                    MIREILLE
You said "quiet."

                    OSKAR
Same thing.

She doesn't smile. Leans out an inch, scans, retreats.

                    MIREILLE
Mill's empty. I checked.

                    OSKAR
Checked what?

                    MIREILLE
Everything.

Oskar tugs the dry sock on. Eases a boot over it. Winces.

The wounded man stirs. Mutters. His good hand claws at the tarp.

                    WOUNDED SOLDIER
(delirious)
Mama... the stove's still on...

                    OSKAR
He's talking.

                    MIREILLE
Let him.

                    OSKAR
Should we give him water?

                    MIREILLE
Save it.

She taps a canteen. Hollow. Oskar nods grimly.

                    OSKAR
(to himself)
Three days. Three days since a hot meal.

                    MIREILLE
Four.

                    OSKAR
Thank you, Sergeant.

She almost laughs. Watches the far bank again. A heron lifts from the reeds and flaps downriver, low over the water. Nothing follows it.

                    MIREILLE
(to both)
We cross at dark. Single file. No talking.

                    OSKAR
And him?

                    MIREILLE
We carry him.

                    OSKAR
He's dead weight.

                    MIREILLE
He's a man.

The wounded soldier opens his eyes. Clear for the first time. He looks at Mireille.

                    WOUNDED SOLDIER
Sergeant.

                    MIREILLE
Easy.

                    WOUNDED SOLDIER
Leave me.

                    MIREILLE
No.

                    WOUNDED SOLDIER
I'll slow you.

                    MIREILLE
You'll shut up.

Oskar crawls to the wounded man's side. Presses his palm on the dressing. It's wet. His face changes.

                    OSKAR
Sergeant.

                    MIREILLE
What?

                    OSKAR
He's bleeding out.

She looks. Her jaw sets. She turns away. Fingers dig into the stock of the rifle.

The far bank erupts. A MORTAR round shrieks over the water and lands in the mill yard behind them. Brick, mud, black smoke.

Mireille and Oskar throw themselves flat. The wounded man gasps. His hand goes limp.

Another round. Closer. The wall they hide behind splits down the middle.

                    MIREILLE
Move! Move!

                    OSKAR
He's gone!

                    MIREILLE
Take his tags!

Oskar tears the chain from the dead soldier's neck. Stuffs it in his jacket. The two of them scramble, bent double, down the bank toward the waterwheel.

MIREILLE
(muttering, rifle up)
Merde, merde, merde.

They splash into the shallows as machine-gun fire stitches the water behind them.

                    SGT. DUVAL
(shouting over the noise)
Stay low! Follow me!

                    OSKAR
Where?

                    SGT. DUVAL
Anywhere that isn't here!

She plunges into the current. He follows, holding his rifle overhead. Under the waterwheel they vanish into the mist.
